§§ `נספח ב' — לוח זמנים ונהלי ועדת המינויים`

-- The timetable: the list of candidates published in the school year's
-- first week; applications by 1 December; the committee's approved list to
-- the division by 30 April; it ends its work by 31 May, its decisions in
-- force back to 1 January of that academic year.
@ref akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_1 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_1__para_1 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_1__para_2 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_1__para_3 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_1__para_4
`the committee's list reaches the division by, of 22.5.1997` MEANS "30 April"
`the committee ends its work by, of 22.5.1997` MEANS "31 May"

-- Chapter א': a standing secretariat at every college: it tells the
-- teachers by 30 November they may apply, publishes who may, confirms an
-- application in writing within 21 days, and prepares the files (the
-- superiors' opinions, the students' formal feedback on at least half the
-- courses of each of the last three years, other opinions), serves the
-- internal committees, has everyone involved sign confidentiality and keeps
-- the minutes.
@ref akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_2 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_2/p1 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_2/p2 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_2__para_1 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_2__para_2 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_2__para_3 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_2__para_4 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_2__para_4__subpara_a akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_2__para_4__subpara_b akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_2__para_4__subpara_c akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_2__para_4__subpara_d akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_2__para_4__subpara_e akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_2__para_4__subpara_f
`telling the teachers they may apply, of 22.5.1997` MEANS
    PARTY `the appointments committee's secretariat`
    MUST  `notify the teachers they may apply, by 30 November`

`confirming an application, of 22.5.1997` MEANS
    PARTY `the appointments committee's secretariat`
    MUST  `confirm receipt of an application within 21 days`
    WITHIN 21

`the share of the courses the students' feedback covers, of 22.5.1997` MEANS 50%

-- akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_2__para_4__subpara_f/p2 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_3__para_6/p2 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_4__para_4/p3 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_5__para_3__subpara_d/p2 Fax headers; no rule.

-- Chapter ב': a quorum of 5 of the 6 with the candidate's field; a
-- majority, and on a tie a member of the pool (9.ד.5, the corpus's sic for
-- "9.ד.4") joins a new hearing; the deliberations confidential, everyone
-- involved signs; a separate minute per application, each position in it,
-- every decision reasoned in detail and signed; the decision in writing to
-- the teacher, the institution and the division.
@ref akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_3 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_3__para_1 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_3__para_1__subpara_a akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_3__para_1__subpara_b akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_3__para_2 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_3__para_3 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_3__para_4 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_3__para_5 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_3__para_6
GIVEN `for`, `against` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a member of the pool joins, of 22.5.1997` `for` `against` IF
    `for` EQUALS `against`

-- Chapter ג': the committee takes the applications in the order filed,
-- may set up subcommittees; each institution makes a form (personal
-- details, education, seniority, training, experience, projects,
-- initiatives, programmes, teams, research, publications, recent
-- training, anything else), with the documents that support it.
-- akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_4 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_4/p1 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_4__para_1 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_4__para_2 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_4__para_3 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_4__para_3/p2 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_4__para_3/p3 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_4__para_3/p4 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_4__para_3/p5 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_4__para_3/p6 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_4__para_3/p7 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_4__para_3/p8 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_4__para_3/p9 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_4__para_3/p10 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_4__para_3/p11 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_4__para_3/p12 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_4__para_3/p13 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_4__para_3/p14 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_4__para_3/p15 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_4__para_4 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_4__para_4/p2 The committee's working order and the application form's contents; procedure with no rule to compute.

-- Chapter ד': the elections of the teachers' members: 3 of management and
-- 3 of the 4 elected sit; the teachers' committee sets up an election
-- committee (a chair and three, one from each of the four groups), none of
-- them a candidate; it gets the lists of who may vote (9.ז) and who may be
-- elected (§4), each teacher in his main field by position (on a tie, his
-- choice); it publishes them two months before the vote at least; an
-- appeal within two weeks, decided in writing within 10 days; the final
-- list a month before at least; then it writes to every voter with the
-- forms and the rules; candidacy within 10 working days of the final
-- list; the candidates published 8 working days before the vote; a ballot
-- committee of 3 non-candidates, four boxes, one per field, open with two
-- of them present; the results approved, published and passed on. A
-- working day is a day the college operates. The inter-college
-- committee's rules come later.
@ref akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_5 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_5__para_1 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_5__para_1__subpara_a akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_5__para_1__subpara_b akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_5__para_2 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_5__para_2__subpara_a akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_5__para_2__subpara_b akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_5__para_2__subpara_c akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_5__para_2__subpara_d akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_5__para_2__subpara_d__cls_1 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_5__para_2__subpara_d__cls_2 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_5__para_2__subpara_e akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_5__para_3 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_5__para_3__subpara_a akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_5__para_3__subpara_b akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_5__para_3__subpara_c akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_5__para_3__subpara_d akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_5__para_3__subpara_e akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_5__para_3__subpara_e/p2 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_5__para_3__subpara_e__cls_1 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_5__para_3__subpara_e__cls_2 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_5__para_3__subpara_e__cls_3 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_5__para_4 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_5__para_4__subpara_a akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_5__para_4__subpara_b akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_5__para_4__subpara_c akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_5__para_5 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_5__para_5__subpara_a akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_5__para_5__subpara_b akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_5__para_5__subpara_c akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_5__para_5__subpara_d akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_5__para_5__subpara_e akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_5__para_5__subpara_f akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_5__para_5__subpara_f__cls_1 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_5__para_5__subpara_f__cls_2 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_5__para_5__subpara_f__cls_3 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_5__para_6 akn:att_2__hc_1__hc_5__para_7
`days before the vote the voters are published, at least, of 22.5.1997` MEANS 60
`days to appeal the list, of 22.5.1997` MEANS 14
`days to decide an appeal, of 22.5.1997` MEANS 10
`working days to stand after the final list, of 22.5.1997` MEANS 10
`working days before the vote the candidates are published, of 22.5.1997` MEANS 8

GIVEN `the college operates that day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a working day of annex ב' of 22.5.1997` `the college operates that day` IF
    `the college operates that day`

§§ `סיכום לוואי`

-- akn:att_3__hc_1/p1 The corpus's note on where the side letter is in the scan; no rule.
-- akn:att_3__hc_1/p2 akn:att_3__hc_1/p3 akn:att_3__hc_1/p4 akn:att_3__hc_1/p5 akn:att_3__hc_1/p6 The letter's place, date (22 May 1997), reference and title, and its recital that it follows the agreement under §24 of 11.5.93 and §20 of 19.9.94; no rule.
-- akn:attachments/p1 akn:attachments/t1 akn:attachments/p2 akn:attachments/p3 The letter's signatures, an illegible hand and the Ministry's address; no rule.

-- 1: the colleges' pedagogic dismissal procedure follows the minute of
-- the conditions-of-service subcommittee of 14.12.95, signed as a
-- memorandum and part of the agreement — the summary annexed after this
-- letter, encoded below.
-- 2: tenure at a college needs three years' trial; in single, exceptional
-- cases, on pedagogic grounds only, by the institution's teaching
-- committee with הסתדרות המורים's consent, one year more. 3: overuse of
-- the extension goes to the parity committee. 4: the funding is the
-- supreme parity committee's. 5: these rules hold only where the
-- agreement is applied in full. ¶7: the letter exhausts dismissal and
-- tenure at the colleges.
@ref akn:att_3__hc_1__para_1 akn:att_3__hc_1__para_2 akn:att_3__hc_1__para_3 akn:att_3__hc_1__para_4 akn:att_3__hc_1__para_5 akn:att_3__hc_1/p7
GIVEN `extended on pedagogic grounds with the union's consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `years of trial before tenure at a college, of 22.5.1997` `extended on pedagogic grounds with the union's consent` IS
    IF `extended on pedagogic grounds with the union's consent` THEN 4 ELSE 3

§§ `סיכום הליך פיטורין פדגוגיים`

-- akn:att_4__hc_1/p1 The corpus's note on where the summary is in the scan; no rule.
-- akn:att_4__hc_1/p2 The summary's title; no rule.
-- akn:att_4__hc_1__para_7__subpara_c/p2 A fax header; no rule.
-- akn:attachments/p4 akn:attachments/t2 akn:attachments/p5 The summary's signatures and an illegible hand; no rule.

-- 1: a college's management that concludes a teacher's work should end on
-- pedagogic grounds (wear, unfitness, inability to teach …) brings it in
-- writing to the institution's teaching committee, which serves to assess
-- the teacher's work. 2: copies to the Ministry's division, the teacher's
-- representative organisation and the teacher.
@ref akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1/p2 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2
`bringing a pedagogic dismissal, of 22.5.1997` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `bring a pedagogic dismissal before the college's teaching committee`

-- 3: if the teaching committee finds grounds, it recommends a warning to
-- the teacher, through the division to the director-general for a State
-- employee, to the association's or owner's chair for theirs; the warning
-- period starts. 4: in it, the teacher is assessed by the division's
-- professional and the institution's (not of the teaching committee);
-- a request to end the work goes to the parity committee only on clear
-- reports from each. 5: the opinion rests on students' feedback and four
-- separate visits by the two, two a semester, with written reports and
-- clear recommendations. 6: the warning goes to the parity committee at
-- the school year's end, by the end of July, naming what is wrong and
-- that in the coming year the teacher is under close supervision, and
-- that with no improvement his dismissal will be recommended.
@ref akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3/p2 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_4 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_4__subpara_a akn:att_4__hc_1__para_4__subpara_b akn:att_4__hc_1__para_4/p2 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_5 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_6
`sending the warning, of 22.5.1997` MEANS
    PARTY `the college's teaching committee`
    MUST  `send the warning to the parity committee by the end of July`

`visits in the year under supervision, of 22.5.1997` MEANS 4

-- 7: the parity committee: the institution's or the owner's
-- representatives, the Ministry's (the division, teaching personnel,
-- conditions of service, the accountant, the institution's training
-- division) and the teacher's organisation's. 8: it decides at its
-- discretion, finally; a decision to end the work ends it at the end of
-- that school year. 9: the notice is sent by the director-general for a
-- State employee, by the association's or owner's chair for theirs.
@ref akn:att_4__hc_1__para_7 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_7__subpara_a akn:att_4__hc_1__para_7__subpara_b akn:att_4__hc_1__para_7__subpara_b__cls_1 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_7__subpara_b__cls_2 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_7__subpara_b__cls_3 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_7__subpara_b__cls_4 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_7__subpara_b__cls_5 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_7__subpara_c akn:att_4__hc_1__para_8 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_8/p2 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_8/p3 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_9
`deciding a pedagogic dismissal, of 22.5.1997` MEANS
    PARTY `the parity committee`
    MAY   `decide a pedagogic dismissal`

-- The work ends on the last day of the school year of the decision; the
-- notice the procedure gives is the days from the notice to that day.
-- Days are counted as day numbers (DATE_SERIAL), as the Advance Notice
-- Law's §2(ג) counts them.
GIVEN `the day the notice is sent` IS A DATE, `the last day of the school year of the decision` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `days of notice the pedagogic dismissal of 22.5.1997 gives` `the day the notice is sent` `the last day of the school year of the decision` IS
    max 0 (DATE_SERIAL `the last day of the school year of the decision` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the day the notice is sent`)

§§ `Worked examples`

GIVEN `fixed position` IS A NUMBER, `academic position` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `college teacher of 22.5.1997`
DECIDE `a tenured lecturer of 22.5.1997 at` `fixed position` `academic position` IS
    `college teacher of 22.5.1997` WITH
        `teaches at a college with the Council's permit`                    IS TRUE
        `on the teaching employees' scale, under their agreements`          IS TRUE
        `tenured at the college`                                            IS TRUE
        `holds a second or third degree`                                    IS TRUE
        `holds a salary grade equivalent to a second or third degree`       IS FALSE
        `held a recognised academic appointment at an institution of higher education` IS FALSE
        `fixed position at the college`                                     IS `fixed position`
        `fixed position in the academic tracks`                             IS `academic position`
        `rank now`                                                          IS `lecturer in an academic institution for teacher training`
        `years worked at the college`                                       IS 9
        `years in the rank now`                                             IS 3
        `recommended for senior lecturer A by the college's committee`      IS FALSE

`a tenured lecturer of 22.5.1997 at 80%` MEANS `a tenured lecturer of 22.5.1997 at` 0.8 0.6

#ASSERT `the agreement of 22.5.1997 applies to` `a tenured lecturer of 22.5.1997 at 80%`
#ASSERT `a candidate for promotion under 22.5.1997` `a tenured lecturer of 22.5.1997 at 80%`
#ASSERT `may apply for the rank under §8 of 22.5.1997` `a tenured lecturer of 22.5.1997 at 80%` `senior lecturer in an academic institution for teacher training`
#ASSERT NOT `may apply for the rank under §8 of 22.5.1997` `a tenured lecturer of 22.5.1997 at 80%` `senior lecturer A in an academic institution for teacher training`
#ASSERT NOT `meets §4 of 22.5.1997 for the rank` `a tenured lecturer of 22.5.1997 at 80%` `senior lecturer A in an academic institution for teacher training`
#ASSERT NOT `the rank of 22.5.1997 is cancelled` `a tenured lecturer of 22.5.1997 at 80%` FALSE FALSE 0
#ASSERT `the rank of 22.5.1997 is cancelled` `a tenured lecturer of 22.5.1997 at 80%` TRUE FALSE 0
#ASSERT `the rank of 22.5.1997 is cancelled` (`a tenured lecturer of 22.5.1997 at` 0.7 0.6) FALSE FALSE 0
#ASSERT NOT `the rank of 22.5.1997 is cancelled` (`a tenured lecturer of 22.5.1997 at` 0.7 0.6) FALSE FALSE 1
#ASSERT `the rank of 22.5.1997 is cancelled` `a tenured lecturer of 22.5.1997 at 80%` FALSE FALSE 3

-- A lecturer on a combined salary of 10,000 at 80%: 7.5% of it by his
-- position, 600; at 120%, 900.
#ASSERT `the rank's supplement of 22.5.1997` `lecturer in an academic institution for teacher training` 10000 0.8 EQUALS 600
#ASSERT `the rank's supplement of 22.5.1997` `lecturer in an academic institution for teacher training` 10000 1.2 EQUALS 900
#ASSERT `the rank's supplement of 22.5.1997` `teacher, the basic rank of 22.5.1997` 10000 1 EQUALS 0

#ASSERT `a rank of 22.5.1997 runs from` 1998 EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1999
#ASSERT `a rank of 22.5.1997 runs from` 1997 EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 1997
#ASSERT NOT `the last supplement counts toward the budgetary pension, of 22.5.1997` 3 FALSE
#ASSERT `the last supplement counts toward the budgetary pension, of 22.5.1997` 3 TRUE

-- §7: a senior lecturer at 66%, half of it academic, by the exception;
-- never senior lecturer A; not in the formation stage but in a unique field.
`a tenured teacher of 22.5.1997 at 66%` MEANS `a tenured lecturer of 22.5.1997 at` 0.66 0.5
#ASSERT `may hold the rank by the exception of §7 of 22.5.1997` `a tenured teacher of 22.5.1997 at 66%` `senior lecturer in an academic institution for teacher training` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `may hold the rank by the exception of §7 of 22.5.1997` `a tenured teacher of 22.5.1997 at 66%` `senior lecturer A in an academic institution for teacher training` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `may hold the rank by the exception of §7 of 22.5.1997` `a tenured teacher of 22.5.1997 at 66%` `senior lecturer in an academic institution for teacher training` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `may hold the rank by the exception of §7 of 22.5.1997` `a tenured teacher of 22.5.1997 at 66%` `senior lecturer in an academic institution for teacher training` TRUE TRUE

-- §16 by §7: a tenured teacher with an equivalent grade at 80%, 60% of it
-- academic, may be a senior lecturer by §7's terms, never senior lecturer
-- A; §4 does not reach him.
`a tenured teacher of 22.5.1997 with an equivalent grade` MEANS
    `college teacher of 22.5.1997` WITH
        `teaches at a college with the Council's permit`                    IS TRUE
        `on the teaching employees' scale, under their agreements`          IS TRUE
        `tenured at the college`                                            IS TRUE
        `holds a second or third degree`                                    IS FALSE
        `holds a salary grade equivalent to a second or third degree`       IS TRUE
        `held a recognised academic appointment at an institution of higher education` IS FALSE
        `fixed position at the college`                                     IS 0.8
        `fixed position in the academic tracks`                             IS 0.6
        `rank now`                                                          IS `lecturer in an academic institution for teacher training`
        `years worked at the college`                                       IS 9
        `years in the rank now`                                             IS 3
        `recommended for senior lecturer A by the college's committee`      IS FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `a candidate for promotion under 22.5.1997` `a tenured teacher of 22.5.1997 with an equivalent grade`
#ASSERT `an equivalent grade may hold the rank under §16 of 22.5.1997` `a tenured teacher of 22.5.1997 with an equivalent grade` `senior lecturer in an academic institution for teacher training` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `an equivalent grade may hold the rank under §16 of 22.5.1997` `a tenured teacher of 22.5.1997 with an equivalent grade` `senior lecturer A in an academic institution for teacher training` FALSE

-- The procedure's notice: decided and sent on 1.7, the year ending on
-- 31.8, gives 61 days; sent on 20.8, 11.
#ASSERT `days of notice the pedagogic dismissal of 22.5.1997 gives` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 1999) (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 1999) EQUALS 61
#ASSERT `days of notice the pedagogic dismissal of 22.5.1997 gives` (DATE_FROM_DMY 20 8 1999) (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 1999) EQUALS 11

§§ `Property checks`

-- §5: for every rank the weights add up to 100%; the starred criterion of
-- each promotion rank but senior teacher weighs 40%.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN r YIELD `the weights of 22.5.1997 add up, for` r EQUALS 100%) `the promotion ranks of 22.5.1997`
#ASSERT all (GIVEN r YIELD
                r EQUALS `senior teacher in an academic institution for teacher training`
                OR `the weight of a criterion of 22.5.1997` r (`the criterion the table stars for` r) EQUALS 40%)
            `the promotion ranks of 22.5.1997`

-- §6: the four shares and the basic rank's least make up the whole.
`the shares of §6 of 22.5.1997 and the basic rank's least` MEANS
    sum (map `the most of the candidates a rank of 22.5.1997 may hold` `the promotion ranks of 22.5.1997`)
        PLUS `the fewest of the candidates in the basic rank, of 22.5.1997`
#ASSERT `the shares of §6 of 22.5.1997 and the basic rank's least` EQUALS 100%

-- §11: the supplement rises with the rank; §14.ד: no rank takes more in a
-- year of the formation stage than §6 lets it hold.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN r YIELD
                    `the supplement rate of a rank of 22.5.1997` r GREATER THAN `the supplement rate of a rank of 22.5.1997` (`the rank below, of 22.5.1997` r)
                AND all (GIVEN y YIELD
                            `the most of the candidates a rank of 22.5.1997 may take in a year of the formation stage` r y
                                AT MOST `the most of the candidates a rank of 22.5.1997 may hold` r)
                        (LIST 1, 2, 3))
            `the promotion ranks of 22.5.1997`

-- §§9–10: the committees as composed are the size the agreement gives them.
#ASSERT `of the management, of 22.5.1997` PLUS `of the elected who sit, of 22.5.1997` EQUALS `the members of the college's appointments committee, of 22.5.1997`
#ASSERT `the inter-college committee as 10.ה composes it, of 22.5.1997` EQUALS `the members of the inter-college committee, of 22.5.1997`
#ASSERT `the members of an ad hoc appointments committee, of 22.5.1997` EQUALS 5
